.TH MANGO-SETTINGS 1 "2025" "mango-settings 2.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mango-settings \- graphical settings manager for the MangoWM Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mango-settings
[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIPAGE\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-\-list-pages\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mango-settings
is a GTK 3 application that edits MangoWM's configuration files
(\fI~/.config/mango/config.conf\fR and the files it includes) while
preserving comments, ordering, symlinks and permissions.
.PP
Changes are written atomically after the original files have been backed
up to \fI~/.cache/mango-settings/backups/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-page " " \fIPAGE\fR
Open the given page. Accepts the page key, its title, or a
dash/underscore spelling (for example
\fBwindow\-behavior\fR or \fB"Window behavior"\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Edit \fIFILE\fR instead of the default \fI~/.config/mango/config.conf\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the loaded configuration and exit. Prints include problems
(cycles, missing files, depth loops) and exits with status 1 on errors.
No GUI or display is required.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-pages
List every page name and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate the MangoWM configuration, the application's own settings
(\fI~/.config/mango-settings/settings.ini\fR) and the backup directory.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY
The GUI needs a running Wayland or X session. Use \fB\-\-check\fR,
\fB\-\-list\-pages\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR headlessly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mango/config.conf
MangoWM's main configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mango-settings/settings.ini
Mango Settings' own preferences (theme, window geometry, blur).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mango-settings/backups/
Timestamped backups written before every save.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Validation errors with \fB\-\-check\fR, or a runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mango (1),
.BR mmsg (1)
.PP
